abstract: >-
  Minimal unbiased compositional change generates the Gaussian source
  underlying the compact internal construction. Its gauge and matter content
  together with its scalar sector determine effective couplings and mass
  scales through common spectral responses and kinetic normalizations. Joint
  screening selects three matter copies. Shell support and position retention
  select the finite response level R=5. The transverse-traceless endpoint at
  this level has a unique positive root. Eliminating shared transfer
  parameters gives a relation among six geometric fermion masses and
  correlates the electron and electroweak scales. It also gives two
  cosmological ratios independent of the common neutrino mass normalization.
  Finite one-loop matching implements the generated Fermi condition together
  with the top and Higgs conditions in a common action and gives a Born top
  width of 1.53445 GeV. A local nonlinear source–potential system and an
  auxiliary-radius model realize source feedback. The latter has positive
  reduced propagation and a matter-phase clock on a specified finite
  cosmological interval. The fixed DESI DR2 distance comparison gives
  χ²=29.5088 for thirteen components and p=0.00554. This identifies tension in
  the adopted cosmological mapping. Spectral and quadrature bounds control the
  finite-response calculation. Mass-scheme matching and thermal approximations
  enter the physical comparisons separately.
